// `++=` appends to the list in place, yet its result is still written back with
// `SetGlobal`, as any augmented assignment's is: `CallNative` of `++=` on the
// list read into r2 and the `[2]` in r3 puts the result in r1, which
// `SetGlobal` stores in `value`.
// compile: stdlib
let value = [1]; value ++= [2];
